@startuml Sequence Diagram - Network Error
title Escenario 3 - Error de Red (Simulator API)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam titleFontSize 11
skinparam ParticipantFontSize 10
skinparam ActorFontSize 10
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam NoteFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceGroupFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceGroupHeaderFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceDividerFontSize 10
skinparam maxMessageSize 150
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #666666

participant "Comercio\n(Backend)" as Comercio
participant "SDK KitPagos" as SDK
participant "Simulator API\n(Fastify)" as SimAPI
participant "Scenario Engine" as Engine

Comercio -> SDK : createPayment(\nCreatePaymentRequest)
SDK -> SimAPI : POST /v1/sim/{gateway}/payments\n(Header x-simulate-scenario: NETWORK_ERROR)
SimAPI -> Engine : resolveScenario(\nheaders, body) ->\n"NETWORK_ERROR"

alt Timeout (SDK no responde dentro del umbral)
  Engine -->x SDK : sin respuesta\n(latencia inyectada > timeout)
  SDK -->x SDK : socket hang up / AbortError
  SDK -> SDK : mapear a KitPagosError(\nGATEWAY_TIMEOUT\no CONNECTION_FAILED)
else Error de servidor simulado
  Engine --> SimAPI : 5xx (Wompi/MP/Rapyd) o 200 con\ncode="ERROR" (Kushki)
  SimAPI --> SDK : respuesta de error nativa
  SDK -> SDK : mapear codigo HTTP o body.code\n-> KitPagosErrorCode
end

SDK -->x Comercio : throw KitPagosError{\ncode, gateway,\noriginalPayload}

note bottom
  Kushki SIEMPRE devuelve HTTP 200: el adaptador debe leer body.code/body.error,
  NO el status HTTP, para decidir GATEWAY_SERVER_ERROR. Rapyd SI usa codigos HTTP
  diferenciados (200/400/401), a diferencia de Kushki
  (docs.rapyd.net/en/list-payments.html) — leer tambien body.status.error_code
  para el detalle.
end note

@enduml
